WEBVTT


00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.448
- Yes?
- Andrew Wyke?


00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.589
That's right.


00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.051
I'm Milo Tindle.


00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:09.024
Oh, yes, good.


00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.258
Glad to meet you.


00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.164
You got the train to Charlebury,
did you?


00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.671
- I drove.
- Oh, you drove?


00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.001
That's my car.


00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.076
Oh, the little one?


00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:28.009
- Not the big one.
- No, the big one's mine.


00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.115
What do you think of it?


00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.520
- Very handsome.
- Yeah.


00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.849
It is, isn't it?


00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.288
Come in.


00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.862
I was watching a video
of one of my books on television.


00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.107
Like the house?


00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.768
Extraordinary.


00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:03.712
You know who designed it,
who the interior decorator was?


00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.249
Yes, your wife.


00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.886
You knew?


00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.749
Yes, I knew.


00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.948
I'll show you around later.


00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.786
Have a drink. I'm drinking vodka.


00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.622
- Scotch, please.
- Scotch.


00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:20.288
Milo, what an interesting name.
You're a foreigner, I take it?


00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.957
My father's Italian.


00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:25.366
Milo sounds Hungarian.


00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.199
Does it?


00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.765
Here's your Scotch.


00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.038
Cheers.


00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:36.011
Cheers.


00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:40.811
You sure your father
isn't Hungarian?


00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.854
Well, if he is,
he's kept it a dead secret for years.


00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.651
- And your mother?
- English.


00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.317
So you're a kind of half-breed?


00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.394
Sit down.


00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.568
- Thanks for agreeing to see me.
- Not at all.


00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.835
I didn't know you wrote plays
for television.


00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:07.479
I don't. I write crime novels.
You must know that.


00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:08.671
I had heard.


00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:12.340
But sometimes they're adapted
for television by other people.


00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.782
You know what the word
adapted means, I take it?


00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.785
Adapted?


00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:19.015
They may not have such a word
in Italian.


00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.059
- I speak English.
- Good.


00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.686
Come and have a look
at my special book room.


00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.670
These are all my novels.


00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.868
You've read them, I suppose?


00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.910
Afraid not.


00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.048
Good God, no?
What about this one?


00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:45.514
<i>- Rat in a Trap?
- No.</i>


00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.312
<i>- The Obelisk?
- No.</i>


00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.511
<i>- Blackout?
- No.</i>


00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:51.179
<i>- Dead Fish?
- Afraid not.</i>


00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.222
God, you're one in a million.


00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:57.386
- Am I?
- Oh, absolu... I'm very popular.


00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.588
You see this shelf?


00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.723
Translations.


00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:05.337
French, Dutch, German.


00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:07.302
You speak Dutch yourself, do you?


00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.636
Yes, how did you know?
I have a Dutch uncle.


00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.744
Can't see any Italian translations.


00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:17.110
No, they're a funny lot, the Italians.
Culture isn't really their thing.


00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.648
Their salami's good, though.


00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.548
- Oh, is it?
- Italian salami? Best in the world.


00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.552
Did you bring any with you?


00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.850
- No, I left it at home.
- Oh, shame.


00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.788
We're gonna have it
for supper tonight.


00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.825
With a couple of bottles
of Valpolicella.


00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:32.965
- We?
- Maggie and me.


00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.101
Your glass is empty.
What were you drinking, vodka?


00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.795
- Scotch.
- Scotch.


00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.745
<i>I want to come to the point.</i>


00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.250
<i>Point? What point?</i>


00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.321
<i>Are you gonna give Maggie
a divorce?</i>


00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.821
<i>And if not, why not?</i>


00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:01.425
<i>Yeah, yes, yes, we'll come to that.</i>


00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.585
<i>She thinks
you're being unreasonable.</i>


00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:05.355
<i>So do I.</i>


00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.728
<i>She's never coming back to you,
so why not just give her the divorce?</i>


00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:12.302
<i>It'll do her good to wait for five years.
Good for her character.</i>


00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:14.997
<i>You're going to make her wait
five years?</i>


00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:18.666
<i>- That's the law. The law of the land.
- But that's pure spite.</i>


00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:23.111
<i>Anyway, we'll get back to that,
perhaps. Have your drink first.</i>


00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.780
<i>What do you do, by the way?</i>


00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.513
<i>I'm an actor.</i>


00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.090
<i>Good God. Are you really?</i>


00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:36.023
<i>I thought Maggie said
you were a hairdresser.</i>


00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:38.322
<i>She must have been talking
about someone else.</i>


00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:39.988
<i>You mean another friend?</i>


00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:41.633
<i>Another friend?</i>


00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.564
<i>She tends to have
more than one friend.</i>


00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:44.998
<i>- Does she?
- Oh, yes.</i>


00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.570
<i>I'm her only friend.</i>


00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.263
<i>She must be lonely.</i>


00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.068
<i>She's not.</i>


00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:53.940
<i>Acting is a pretty precarious
profession, isn't it?</i>


00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:56.411
<i>What are you acting in
at the moment?</i>


00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.447
<i>I'm out of work.</i>


00:06:58.618 --> 00:06:59.642
<i>Poor chap.</i>


00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:02.549
<i>I drive cars now and again,
chauffeuring.</i>


00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:05.156
<i>- Oh, tough life.
- I keep my head above water.</i>


00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:08.890
<i>What sort of parts do you play?</i>


00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:12.221
Killers, mostly.


00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:15.458
Sex maniacs, perverts.


00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:17.227
But you're so charming.


00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:20.031
Yes, I know.
Anyway, what about this divorce?


00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:22.436
What's your position, exactly?


00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:25.076
All in good time.


00:07:33.953 --> 00:07:35.580
Come in.


00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:45.631
Have a seat.
Make yourself comfortable.


00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:54.129
I understand you're fucking my wife.


00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:56.434
- That's right.
- Right.


00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:58.270
Yes, right.


00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.571
- So we've cleared that up.
- We have.


00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:02.941
- I thought you might deny it.
- Why would I deny it?


00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.982
- Well, she is my wife.
- Yes, but she's fucking me.


00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:08.848
Oh, she's fucking you too?
Well, I'll be buggered.


00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:11.418
- Sorry.
- Yes, it's mutual.


00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:13.286
- You take turns?
- We fuck each other.


00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:17.327
- That's what people do.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. I follow.


00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:22.826
- We're in love.
- You're in love?


00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:24.498
That's right.


00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.266
Let me top you up.


00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:41.949
I heard a rumor
that you wanted to marry her.


00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.089
- That can't be true, can it?
- Why not?


00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:47.158
In this day and age,
is marriage absolutely necessary?


00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:48.384
Isn't it a bit old hat?


00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:50.426
- Is it?
- It's a mug's game.


00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:53.224
I wouldn't go near it if I were you.
You can't marry her.


00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:55.594
You can't marry her
because she's married to me.


00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:57.463
Unless I divorce her, of course.


00:08:57.637 --> 00:08:59.662
- And are you?
- Am I what?


00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:00.931
Going to divorce her?


00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:03.200
Are you really gonna
make her wait five years?


00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:06.277
- She wants to know.
- To be honest, I can't wait.


00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:09.643
But there are one or two things
I'd like to clear up first.


00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:14.479
For example, I've never heard
of an Italian called Tindle.


00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:16.121
My father's name is Tindolini.


00:09:16.289 --> 00:09:19.622
Now, that's lovely.
That's like a little bell.


00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:22.818
Why don't you go back to Tindolini?
It suits you.


00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:24.462
- You think so?
- Yes.


00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:29.260
So if and when you marry Maggie,
she'll be Maggie Tindolini.


00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:31.903
Do you get a kick out of that?


00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:34.836
What name do you act under?
Tindle or Tindolini?


00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:36.998
- Tindle.
- Why have I never heard of you?


00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:38.507
You will before long.


00:09:38.678 --> 00:09:40.543
- Really?
- In spades.


00:09:40.713 --> 00:09:42.374
- That sounds threatening.
- Does it?


00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:44.015
Doesn't it?


00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:49.649
Why don't we get down
to brass tacks?


00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:52.757
Brass tacks, yes. Why not?


00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.324
This is the way I see it.


00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.090
Come upstairs.


00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:02.099
I want to show you something.


00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:09.167
Are you all right in elevators?


00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:15.307
It won't make you sick
or anything, will it?


00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.360
This is our bedroom.


00:10:34.367 --> 00:10:40.636
And this is my wife's dressing room.


00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:45.138
She left a few dresses.
Couldn't be bothered to pick them up.


00:10:45.311 --> 00:10:48.644
They're worth thousands.
Thousands.


00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:52.477
This leather coat alone
is worth 5000 quid.


00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:56.247
So you see, the thing is this.
Sit down.


00:10:59.558 --> 00:11:02.026
The thing is this,
my wife spends money like water.


00:11:02.194 --> 00:11:06.563
So if you're not careful,
she'll eat you out of house and home.


00:11:06.732 --> 00:11:09.997
She was born to luxury, you know.
Jamaica, the Ritz, the Swiss Alps.


00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:13.969
What are you?
Out-of-work actor, part-time chauffeur.


00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:17.166
You're out of your depth, old boy.
You're on a hiding to nothing.


00:11:17.343 --> 00:11:19.004
If you think you're broke now...


00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:22.375
...you'll be 10 times broker
by the time she's finished with you.


00:11:22.548 --> 00:11:24.345
She'll have your guts for garters.


00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:28.911
- She's in love with me.
- Oh, never trust in love, chum.


00:11:29.088 --> 00:11:32.057
Love will kick you up the arse
as soon as look at you.


00:11:32.224 --> 00:11:35.751
One minute, it's love,
10 minutes later, it's contempt.


00:11:35.928 --> 00:11:37.555
That's your own experience, is it?


00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.528
Oh, no, no, no, that's observation.


00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.998
Don't forget, I'm a novelist.


00:11:43.169 --> 00:11:45.637
I observe people.


00:11:46.272 --> 00:11:49.469
What I'm getting at is you won't
be able to give her what she wants.


00:11:49.642 --> 00:11:52.509
So she's gonna leave you,
come back to me.


00:11:52.678 --> 00:11:55.238
I don't want her near me.
That's the last thing I want.


00:11:55.414 --> 00:11:57.245
I've had her up to here.


00:11:57.416 --> 00:12:01.614
Anyway, I've got this lovely mistress.
She runs a sauna in Swindon.


00:12:01.787 --> 00:12:02.845
She's my girl.


00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:05.991
So you see,
I want Maggie to stay with you.


00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:09.025
I want you two
to be together forever.


00:12:09.195 --> 00:12:10.594
But unless you listen to me...


00:12:10.763 --> 00:12:12.958
...the whole thing
will be a fucking disaster...


00:12:13.132 --> 00:12:16.659
...with catastrophic consequences
all round.


00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:22.134
But I have a solution.


00:12:26.011 --> 00:12:29.139
You won't believe
what I'm gonna say.


00:12:31.117 --> 00:12:33.176
What are you gonna say?


00:12:33.352 --> 00:12:35.820
I'm all ears.


00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:37.512
You know something?


00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.590
I'm beginning to respond
to your charm.


00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:41.249
- Get away.
- No, it's true.


00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:44.885
- I'm really touched.
- You should be.


00:12:45.064 --> 00:12:48.363
Tell me, I bet you didn't expect me
to be so intelligent.


00:12:48.534 --> 00:12:50.468
So quick-witted, did you?


00:12:50.636 --> 00:12:52.797
Oh, I did.


00:12:52.972 --> 00:12:54.837
Quite.


00:12:56.242 --> 00:12:58.710
Maggie told you, did she?


00:13:01.947 --> 00:13:04.040
What's your solution?


00:13:08.154 --> 00:13:10.679
It's a close fit, isn't it?


00:13:10.856 --> 00:13:12.687
For two.


00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:24.599
Listen, I'm going
to make you a proposition.


00:13:25.671 --> 00:13:28.037
A few years ago,
I gave her some jewels.


00:13:28.207 --> 00:13:30.539
Amazingly expensive.


00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:34.645
I didn't give them to her, I own them.
They're insured in my name.


00:13:34.814 --> 00:13:38.181
But I let her use them
on special occasions.


00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:41.217
They're worth 1 million pounds.


00:13:41.387 --> 00:13:44.584
They spend half the time in the bank,
half the time in the safe.


00:13:44.757 --> 00:13:49.626
At the moment, they're here
in the house, in the safe.


00:13:49.795 --> 00:13:53.891
And I want you to steal them.


00:13:58.103 --> 00:14:00.628
- Steal them?
- That's right.


00:14:01.207 --> 00:14:04.404
- What the hell do you mean?
- I want you to steal the jewels.


00:14:04.577 --> 00:14:07.011
You want me to steal the jewels?
I don't get it.


00:14:07.179 --> 00:14:09.841
It's simple. You steal the jewels,
sell them abroad...


00:14:10.015 --> 00:14:12.779
...and you live happily ever after
with Maggie.


00:14:12.952 --> 00:14:15.512
I get rid of my wife
and I'll be like a pig in shit.


00:14:15.688 --> 00:14:19.021
You can keep Maggie in the manner
to which she's become accustomed.


00:14:19.191 --> 00:14:22.490
You want me to take part
in a scummy little plot...


00:14:22.661 --> 00:14:24.925
...to defraud your insurance company,
is that it?


00:14:25.097 --> 00:14:26.655
I thought it was quite elegant.


00:14:26.832 --> 00:14:28.390
What do you think I am?


00:14:28.567 --> 00:14:31.127
What the fuck
are you actually talking about?


00:14:31.303 --> 00:14:33.737
- These are real facts.
- This is a joke.


00:14:33.906 --> 00:14:34.930
- No.
- It's also a trap.


00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:36.734
- A trap?
- Yes. You think I'm a fool.


00:14:36.909 --> 00:14:38.171
Well, are you?


00:14:38.344 --> 00:14:39.675
- It doesn't hold up.
- Why not?


00:14:39.845 --> 00:14:43.337
They're worth a million pounds. You'd
get a fraction of that from any fence.


00:14:43.515 --> 00:14:46.643
I have already contacted
a friend of mine in Amsterdam.


00:14:46.819 --> 00:14:52.416
And he will give you
800,000 pounds tax-free.


00:14:52.591 --> 00:14:54.616
Now, think about it.


00:14:54.793 --> 00:14:57.387
Eight hundred thousand pounds...


00:14:57.563 --> 00:14:59.622
...tax-free.


00:15:02.301 --> 00:15:03.529
Why would he do that?


00:15:03.702 --> 00:15:06.466
When you steal the jewels,
you will also steal the receipts.


00:15:06.639 --> 00:15:10.336
So he'll have title to the jewels
as well as the jewels themselves...


00:15:10.509 --> 00:15:13.137
...so that when he sells them,
he gets full value.


00:15:16.582 --> 00:15:18.447
Got it?


00:15:18.617 --> 00:15:20.414
Think about it.


00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:22.713
Take your time.


00:15:40.673 --> 00:15:43.540
And why would you do all this?


00:15:43.709 --> 00:15:48.442
Listen, under this crooked exterior,
I am a simple, honest man.


00:15:48.614 --> 00:15:52.243
Every word I've told you is true,
I swear it.


00:15:52.418 --> 00:15:57.913
I want to get rid of my wife,
but I want it to be solid, permanent.


00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:01.116
I don't want her on my back.
I want her to stay on your back.


00:16:01.293 --> 00:16:02.783
This is a frame-up.


00:16:02.962 --> 00:16:05.294
- A frame-up?
- Yes.


00:16:05.464 --> 00:16:08.024
You want to destroy me.


00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.462
You want to see me in jail.


00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:13.127
You want me to do this
and then shop me to the police.


00:16:13.305 --> 00:16:14.533
No, no, no.


00:16:14.707 --> 00:16:19.041
If I shop you, then you'll shop me,
and then we'll both end up in jail.


00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:21.679
No, I take a strictly moral position
on all this.


00:16:21.847 --> 00:16:23.872
My wife is an adulteress.


00:16:24.049 --> 00:16:26.347
Actually,
she should be stoned to death.


00:16:26.518 --> 00:16:29.282
Anyway, it's up to you.
Make up your own mind.


00:16:29.455 --> 00:16:30.854
You're asking me to trust you?


00:16:31.023 --> 00:16:32.991
I don't give a fuck
if you trust me or not.


00:16:33.158 --> 00:16:34.750
This is a simple proposition.


00:16:34.927 --> 00:16:37.555
You have an expensive woman
and no money.


00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.790
You wanna keep the woman,
steal the jewels.


00:16:40.966 --> 00:16:44.800
Why don't you steal the jewels
and give them to me?


