So I'm looking at you
and I'm wondering...


00:52:59.543 --> 00:53:01.807
...what have you done
with the body?


00:53:03.213 --> 00:53:04.942
Where's the body?


00:53:05.715 --> 00:53:07.740
Come on, I need to know.


00:53:08.218 --> 00:53:10.618
Where's the body?
What have you done with the body?


00:53:10.787 --> 00:53:11.811
There's no body.


00:53:11.988 --> 00:53:13.979
Don't fuck about!


00:53:14.157 --> 00:53:15.988
Don't bullshit me.
I won't stand for it.


00:53:16.159 --> 00:53:18.286
Where is it?
In the house or did you shift it?


00:53:18.461 --> 00:53:20.452
There is no body!


00:53:29.105 --> 00:53:32.165
Here, look at this.
You got holes in your walls.


00:53:35.111 --> 00:53:38.046
They're bullet holes.
Live bullet holes.


00:53:38.215 --> 00:53:40.342
I fired two live bullets
to set up the trick...


00:53:40.517 --> 00:53:42.109
...and one blank to complete it.


00:53:42.285 --> 00:53:44.776
It was a game, I told you.
I played it to the hilt.


00:53:44.955 --> 00:53:47.685
It's not worth playing
unless you play it to the hilt.


00:53:47.857 --> 00:53:50.052
- The third shot was a blank?
- That's right.


00:53:50.227 --> 00:53:51.251
- What's that?
- What?


00:53:51.428 --> 00:53:53.487
Blood. Dried blood!


00:53:53.663 --> 00:53:55.927
Some of it's not even dried.
It's still damp.


00:53:56.099 --> 00:53:57.964
- That's impossible.
- That's blood, chum.


00:53:58.134 --> 00:54:00.102
- Whose blood is it?
- It's impossible.


00:54:00.270 --> 00:54:01.760
It was a game. It was a blank.


00:54:01.938 --> 00:54:04.406
No, it was a game
with real bullets and real blood.


00:54:04.574 --> 00:54:05.871
This is a carve-up.


00:54:06.042 --> 00:54:09.842
Let's see what else
is new around here.


00:54:10.413 --> 00:54:12.244
Hello, what's this?


00:54:13.083 --> 00:54:17.076
We've got a shirt, jacket and trousers
in the back of your cupboard.


00:54:17.254 --> 00:54:20.052
Very negligent of you, mate,
unless they're not yours.


00:54:20.223 --> 00:54:24.182
No, I don't think they're yours.
I think they belong to Tindle.


00:54:24.361 --> 00:54:27.125
You say he left the house
after you shot him.


00:54:27.297 --> 00:54:29.197
- Yes.
- Naked?


00:54:29.366 --> 00:54:30.833
I don't know how those got there.


00:54:31.001 --> 00:54:33.401
So you made him strip
before you shot him?


00:54:33.570 --> 00:54:35.561
Part of the humiliation, was it?


00:54:35.739 --> 00:54:37.263
No. The thing is this.


00:54:37.440 --> 00:54:40.466
It might have started as a game,
but it got out of hand.


00:54:40.644 --> 00:54:42.976
The third shot was live!


00:54:43.146 --> 00:54:46.604
It killed him. So where's the body?


00:54:46.783 --> 00:54:48.876
I didn't kill him! He's alive!


00:54:49.052 --> 00:54:51.213
Bollocks. You're a joker, all right.


00:54:51.388 --> 00:54:52.912
A real joker.


00:54:53.089 --> 00:54:54.886
Come on, we're off to the station.


00:54:55.058 --> 00:54:57.652
- There's something very wrong here.
- Hey, dead right.


00:54:57.827 --> 00:55:01.126
I'll tell you what you are.
You're fucked.


00:55:01.598 --> 00:55:02.622
Jesus Christ.


00:55:02.799 --> 00:55:05.063
Don't struggle, chum.
I'll have you for breakfast.


00:55:05.235 --> 00:55:06.566
There's something wrong here.


00:55:06.736 --> 00:55:10.695
You're up shit creek, Wyke.
You're up shit creek without a paddle.


00:55:14.044 --> 00:55:17.536
Look at you. All aquiver.


00:55:18.348 --> 00:55:20.509
Who's the dead duck?


00:55:24.220 --> 00:55:25.653
Jesus Christ.


00:55:29.225 --> 00:55:32.991
You're the dead duck.


00:55:35.699 --> 00:55:41.501
I just sucked you in
and blew you out in little bubbles.


00:55:41.671 --> 00:55:43.138
- It's you.
- It's me, all right.


00:55:43.306 --> 00:55:45.706
You bastard. You stinking bastard.


00:55:45.875 --> 00:55:47.240
Just a little game, Andrew.


00:55:47.410 --> 00:55:49.378
- Just a little game.
- You shit.


00:55:49.546 --> 00:55:52.276
- I thought it might amuse you.
- You're a total shit.


00:55:52.449 --> 00:55:53.780
I know I am.


00:55:53.950 --> 00:55:57.613
- But you're also a genius.
- I know that too.


00:56:00.090 --> 00:56:02.388
When did you do this?
The clothes in the wardrobe?


00:56:02.559 --> 00:56:05.187
- The blood?
- The blood belongs to a pig's liver.


00:56:05.362 --> 00:56:07.523
But when did you do it?
How did you do it?


00:56:07.697 --> 00:56:10.666
I did it last night. I used that ladder.
I heard you snoring.


00:56:10.834 --> 00:56:13.928
Does Maggie know about this?
Your detective, was it her idea?


00:56:14.104 --> 00:56:16.538
- How much does she know?
- She knows nothing about it.


00:56:16.706 --> 00:56:19.834
Entirely my own idea.


00:56:20.009 --> 00:56:23.001
This is a game between us, old boy.


00:56:23.179 --> 00:56:26.046
Between you and me.


00:56:26.216 --> 00:56:28.684
Don't forget, I'm half Italian.


00:56:28.852 --> 00:56:30.513
We go in for revenge.


00:56:43.466 --> 00:56:47.869
After all, you frightened
the life out of me deliberately.


00:56:48.037 --> 00:56:50.904
You fired two live bullets
into the wall...


00:56:51.074 --> 00:56:54.805
...and then you pointed
the gun at me.


00:56:54.978 --> 00:56:57.173
And then you fired.


00:57:01.017 --> 00:57:02.644
I don't like guns.


00:57:03.987 --> 00:57:05.682
They kill you.


00:57:08.958 --> 00:57:10.619
Okay.


00:57:10.794 --> 00:57:13.319
So, what does this make the score?


00:57:14.364 --> 00:57:16.389
You've had your revenge.


00:57:16.566 --> 00:57:20.764
So, what do you reckon?


00:57:21.237 --> 00:57:23.205
One set all?


00:57:23.706 --> 00:57:26.072
No, no, you're way ahead.


00:57:26.876 --> 00:57:31.210
I only teased you with my inspector,
gave you a few goose pimples.


00:57:32.182 --> 00:57:33.774
But you frightened me to death.


00:57:36.019 --> 00:57:38.544
Did you really think
I was going to kill you?


00:57:38.721 --> 00:57:42.350
You fainted, you see.
It was a blank.


00:57:43.493 --> 00:57:46.621
I may be three games up
in the second set.


00:57:46.796 --> 00:57:47.820
If I had killed you...


00:57:47.997 --> 00:57:51.330
...I'd have to bury the body
in the garden or somewhere.


00:57:51.501 --> 00:57:52.525
Too exhausting.


00:57:52.702 --> 00:57:54.135
But you won the first, 6-love.


00:57:58.875 --> 00:58:01.400
So we're a long way
from one set all.


00:58:08.051 --> 00:58:11.077
By the way, I spoke to Maggie.


00:58:11.254 --> 00:58:14.189
I told her all about you.


00:58:14.357 --> 00:58:15.824
She loved it.


00:58:16.960 --> 00:58:18.154
Loved what?


00:58:18.661 --> 00:58:21.425
That I frightened the life out of you.


00:58:21.598 --> 00:58:22.929
That you pissed your pants.


00:58:24.934 --> 00:58:27.425
And that you actually fainted.


00:58:27.604 --> 00:58:30.573
She said to me,
"You mean he actually fainted?"


00:58:30.740 --> 00:58:33.504
I said, "Dead out,
he was scared shitless.


00:58:34.944 --> 00:58:36.468
Went out like a light. "


00:58:37.947 --> 00:58:42.111
She laughed so much,
I thought she was gonna burst.


00:58:46.556 --> 00:58:50.492
Oh, incidentally,
she's coming back to me.


00:58:51.160 --> 00:58:52.491
Oh, is she?


00:58:52.662 --> 00:58:54.391
Yes, that's right.


00:58:54.564 --> 00:58:56.327
You know what she said about you?


00:58:56.499 --> 00:58:57.557
What?


00:58:57.734 --> 00:58:59.031
She said:


00:58:59.202 --> 00:59:02.603
"Faint heart never won fair lady. "


00:59:05.074 --> 00:59:06.234
Is that a fact?


00:59:06.409 --> 00:59:07.706
Yeah.


00:59:09.546 --> 00:59:13.744
Listen, I want to
show you something.


00:59:14.217 --> 00:59:17.516
Go into your study and sit down.


00:59:19.722 --> 00:59:21.280
Go into my study?


00:59:22.792 --> 00:59:24.987
And sit down.


00:59:28.498 --> 00:59:31.467
- What are you doing?
- It's late at night.


00:59:31.634 --> 00:59:33.966
You're reading a book under a lamp.
Read something.


00:59:34.137 --> 00:59:36.697
- What's going on?
- Read a book.


00:59:36.873 --> 00:59:39.273
It's late at night.
You're reading a book.


00:59:39.442 --> 00:59:41.535
You hear something. You look up.


00:59:41.711 --> 00:59:43.508
It's me jumping off the ladder.


00:59:43.680 --> 00:59:45.307
You see me with this gun.


00:59:45.481 --> 00:59:49.508
You're caught like a rat in a trap.
You stare at the gun, you're paralyzed.


00:59:49.686 --> 00:59:51.017
I've come for the jewels.


00:59:51.187 --> 00:59:52.916
- Where is the safe?
- What jewels?


00:59:53.089 --> 00:59:54.454
The jewels. Where's the safe?


00:59:54.624 --> 00:59:56.057
- You know where it is.
- I don't.


00:59:56.225 --> 00:59:58.352
- You don't?
- Don't fuck me about, I mean it.


00:59:58.528 --> 01:00:00.052
Get up.


01:00:00.863 --> 01:00:03.263
You think this gun isn't real?


01:00:05.935 --> 01:00:07.835
Where is it?


01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:11.540
- Upstairs.
- Well, let's go upstairs.


01:00:12.241 --> 01:00:17.543
Get up these stairs
or I'll ram this gun right up your ass.


01:00:17.747 --> 01:00:21.046
- The safe is behind the fish tank.
- How am I gonna get to it?


01:00:21.217 --> 01:00:23.845
Well, you press the button
and the button moves the tank.


01:00:24.020 --> 01:00:26.284
Then press it.


01:00:26.456 --> 01:00:29.016
It's not working. It's out of ord...


01:00:30.426 --> 01:00:31.916
Are you a maniac? You're crazy.


01:00:32.095 --> 01:00:34.791
- Open it.
- I changed the combination yesterday.


01:00:34.964 --> 01:00:37.455
- What is it?
- I forgot. I can't remember.


01:00:37.634 --> 01:00:39.693
- Remember.
- It's the truth. I can't remember.


01:00:39.869 --> 01:00:40.927
Remember!


01:00:44.040 --> 01:00:45.940
What are you doing?
What are you gonna do?


01:00:46.109 --> 01:00:50.273
I've broken into your house because
I know you have jewels in a safe.


01:00:51.114 --> 01:00:53.810
I have inside information.
I want them.


01:00:53.983 --> 01:00:56.383
Remember the combination
and open it.


01:01:03.559 --> 01:01:05.550
It was a blank.


01:01:07.163 --> 01:01:08.653
The next one's real.


01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:29.014
There's a good boy.


01:01:47.103 --> 01:01:49.537
So, what are you writing
at the moment?


01:01:54.477 --> 01:01:56.172
What am I writing?


01:01:56.646 --> 01:01:58.705
Yes, I'm very interested in literature.


01:02:03.186 --> 01:02:05.848
Do you mind if I have a drink?


01:02:06.022 --> 01:02:09.651
Sure. It's your house.


01:02:10.026 --> 01:02:14.224
I'm always interested
in the people I rob.


01:02:14.430 --> 01:02:18.423
Like I'm always interested
in the husbands of the wives I fuck.


01:02:20.036 --> 01:02:21.765
Are you really?


01:02:22.505 --> 01:02:24.166
Well, well.


01:02:25.341 --> 01:02:26.933
Cheers.


01:02:33.483 --> 01:02:38.011
So, what are you writing?


01:02:42.759 --> 01:02:46.422
It's the story of a pathological killer.


01:02:46.596 --> 01:02:49.690
<i>- I call it The Smiling Man.
- Does he come to a bad end?</i>


01:02:49.866 --> 01:02:52.767
He dies during the act of love.
Like countless others.


01:02:52.935 --> 01:02:54.163
Countless others, eh?


01:02:54.337 --> 01:02:56.771
I can see you've researched
the subject thoroughly.


01:02:57.840 --> 01:03:01.241
- What subject?
- Death in orgasm.


01:03:01.410 --> 01:03:05.210
Isn't that a beautiful notion?
To die in the arms of your beloved.


01:03:05.381 --> 01:03:09.044
Can you imagine
anything more poignant?


01:03:09.218 --> 01:03:11.379
- I can't, no.
- No.


01:03:11.554 --> 01:03:15.923
- You're a married man, aren't you?
- Yeah, been married 13 years.


01:03:16.092 --> 01:03:17.354
It was love at first sight.


01:03:17.527 --> 01:03:18.892
- Very moving.
- Yeah.


01:03:19.061 --> 01:03:21.256
And we're still in love.
Like two peas in a pod.


01:03:21.430 --> 01:03:24.024
Someone told me
your wife has a lover.


01:03:24.200 --> 01:03:26.225
- She has, yeah.
- Do you know him?


01:03:26.402 --> 01:03:29.269
No, I've never met him.
He's some sort of Italian.


01:03:29.438 --> 01:03:31.770
Called Tandoori or something.


01:03:31.941 --> 01:03:33.966
One of the Bombay Tandooris?


01:03:34.143 --> 01:03:36.134
You've got it, yeah.


01:03:36.312 --> 01:03:39.179
You know something? I've never met
an artistic burglar before.


01:03:39.348 --> 01:03:41.441
That's fantastic.


01:03:42.685 --> 01:03:44.585
- What's your background?
- Me?


01:03:44.754 --> 01:03:47.188
- You.
- Irish. Connemara.


01:03:47.356 --> 01:03:49.551
Spanish descent.
By way of Uganda.


01:03:49.725 --> 01:03:51.420
My grandparents were slaves.


01:03:51.594 --> 01:03:54.620
My mother was a dark-eyed,
dusky beauty.


01:03:54.797 --> 01:03:58.460
- Were you breastfed?
- Oh, sure, like a baby.


01:04:00.102 --> 01:04:05.734
Shall I tell you what I want you to do
with these jewels?


01:04:06.642 --> 01:04:08.166
What?


01:04:20.556 --> 01:04:25.823
You look so charming.


01:04:32.301 --> 01:04:33.825
How do you want it?


01:04:34.003 --> 01:04:35.595
Like this?


01:04:35.771 --> 01:04:38.137
Or shorter?


01:04:39.208 --> 01:04:43.474
How about this?
Or even shorter like a halter?


01:04:43.646 --> 01:04:47.138
- You're hurting me.
- Oh, am I hurting you?


01:04:47.316 --> 01:04:51.013
- Yes. Don't hurt me.
- Are you sensitive to pain?


01:04:51.187 --> 01:04:53.348
Very. Very.


01:04:53.522 --> 01:04:56.082
I wouldn't want to hurt you,
sweetheart.


01:04:56.259 --> 01:04:58.750
You're too much fun.


01:04:58.928 --> 01:05:02.762
- Am I really?
- Oh, yes. You're wicked.


01:05:02.932 --> 01:05:05.867
I like that. Yeah.


01:05:07.036 --> 01:05:09.095
Do you know something?


01:05:10.273 --> 01:05:13.401
I don't think
these earrings really suit me.


01:05:15.344 --> 01:05:18.472
You're right. Take them off.


01:05:22.451 --> 01:05:24.180
I don't...


01:05:24.353 --> 01:05:29.017
I don't think this bracelet
is really my style either.


01:05:30.826 --> 01:05:33.317
But the necklace is nice.


01:05:34.697 --> 01:05:35.823
I'm not totally sure.


01:05:35.998 --> 01:05:40.901
Listen, you can play with these jewels
until the cows come home.


01:05:41.070 --> 01:05:45.564
They're yours.
Do what you like with them.


01:05:48.144 --> 01:05:51.272
But I thought you'd just stolen them.


01:05:51.447 --> 01:05:53.915
No, no! It was a game!


01:05:54.083 --> 01:05:59.111
It was just a game!
I thought it might amuse you.


01:06:16.272 --> 01:06:17.762
Well...


01:06:19.342 --> 01:06:23.005
Aren't you the wicked one?


01:06:30.419 --> 01:06:31.716
You remember what I said?


01:06:33.389 --> 01:06:36.756
You won the first set, 6-love.
I was 3-love up in the second.


01:06:36.926 --> 01:06:41.363
Well, now it's one set all.


01:06:51.507 --> 01:06:55.034
But who's going to win the third set?


01:06:57.246 --> 01:06:59.339
Remains to be seen.


01:07:18.234 --> 01:07:19.633
You like games, don't you?


01:07:20.936 --> 01:07:23.404
Some. Not all.


01:07:23.572 --> 01:07:26.097
But you like being in charge...


01:07:26.275 --> 01:07:28.038
...of the game?


01:07:29.412 --> 01:07:31.744
Oh, yes. Sure.


01:07:33.449 --> 01:07:36.475
I like a man who wants
to be in charge of things.


01:07:36.685 --> 01:07:39.347
- Do you?
- Yes, I do.


01:07:40.723 --> 01:07:42.918
Listen, you've met my wife, I think.


01:07:44.226 --> 01:07:48.094
I have met her. Yes.


01:07:48.297 --> 01:07:51.130
- Did she say if she had a husband?
- Yes.


01:07:51.300 --> 01:07:53.928
Yeah, she said she had a husband.


01:07:54.737 --> 01:07:57.399
How did she describe him?


01:07:59.375 --> 01:08:01.809
Remote. Cold.


01:08:01.977 --> 01:08:04.878
Malevolent. Spiteful.


01:08:05.347 --> 01:08:07.975
Arrogant. Ruthless.


01:08:08.150 --> 01:08:09.981
Jealous. Paranoid.


01:08:10.152 --> 01:08:14.020
Criminal tendencies.
Mentally unsound.


01:08:14.223 --> 01:08:15.656
That's me, all right.


01:08:20.029 --> 01:08:22.463
You know something?
I like your mind.


01:08:23.165 --> 01:08:25.292
- Do you really?
- It excites me.


01:08:25.701 --> 01:08:27.566
I like the way you go about things.


01:08:29.371 --> 01:08:32.704
You mean you like my style?


01:08:32.875 --> 01:08:35.070
Oh, I like your style.


01:08:35.244 --> 01:08:37.769
I like it very much.


01:08:38.881 --> 01:08:42.578
Look, I want to
make you a proposition.


01:08:43.552 --> 01:08:45.042
What?


01:08:47.389 --> 01:08:49.482
I want to show you something.


01:08:53.729 --> 01:08:57.529
- Can't you put that gun down now?
- No.


01:08:57.700 --> 01:09:00.828
God, you're so strong, so ruthless,
aren't you?


01:09:01.003 --> 01:09:02.027
Yes.


01:09:02.204 --> 01:09:04.968
Have you any idea
what my proposition is going to be?


01:09:05.141 --> 01:09:07.507
- No.
- Are you excited?


01:09:07.676 --> 01:09:08.802
I'd say intrigued.


01:09:08.978 --> 01:09:11.708
I think you're going to be excited
very much.


01:09:11.881 --> 01:09:15.282
This is the guest suite.


01:09:16.919 --> 01:09:20.320
Isn't it nice? Look at the view.


01:09:21.357 --> 01:09:23.484
There's a private bathroom.
A small fridge.


01:09:23.659 --> 01:09:28.858
A bottle of Chilean Chardonnay
is chilling in there at this very moment.


01:09:30.266 --> 01:09:33.064
This suite is uninhabited.


01:09:34.537 --> 01:09:36.129
It has no occupant.


01:09:41.911 --> 01:09:43.640
How would you like it?


01:09:47.082 --> 01:09:48.379
Me?


01:09:50.653 --> 01:09:52.086
Yes, yes.


01:09:52.254 --> 01:09:57.055
I think I've come to the conclusion
that you're my kind of person.


01:10:00.062 --> 01:10:01.586
Am I, now?


01:10:02.164 --> 01:10:04.724
Well, I told you.
I liked your mind. It excited me.


01:10:04.900 --> 01:10:08.768
I need intellectual excitement.


01:10:08.938 --> 01:10:11.236
Intellectual stimulation.


01:10:13.242 --> 01:10:15.142
Well, they don't grow on trees.


01:10:15.911 --> 01:10:18.175
I'm a rich man.


01:10:18.347 --> 01:10:20.406
What do you want to do?


01:10:20.583 --> 01:10:23.211
I can subsidize anything you want.


01:10:24.253 --> 01:10:26.949
You want to open a bookshop
in the village?


01:10:27.756 --> 01:10:31.385
An art gallery?
Or, of course, a little theater.


01:10:31.827 --> 01:10:32.987
You're a wonderful actor.


01:10:33.162 --> 01:10:37.121
